1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,900
A fake parcel text. One tap could leak your card.

2
00:00:04,250 --> 00:00:07,380
PhishProbe checks the link for you — without opening it.

3
00:00:07,750 --> 00:00:11,890
First a fast URL check, then a deep scan in a sandbox on Vultr.

4
00:00:12,250 --> 00:00:17,660
The agent opens it, follows redirects, reads the forms — and calls it: phishing.

5
00:00:18,750 --> 00:00:23,850
Some pages hide text to fool the AI into saying "safe". That itself is a red flag.

6
00:00:24,250 --> 00:00:30,090
Every scan is sandboxed, limited, and destroyed afterward. Blast radius: zero.

7
00:00:30,750 --> 00:00:35,350
A normal link? Green. Calibrated, not paranoid.

8
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:39,410
It's also a Chrome extension — right-click any link to check it.

9
00:00:40,250 --> 00:00:44,780
A badge on every page shows it at a glance: green for safe, red for danger.

10
00:00:46,700 --> 00:00:51,880
PhishProbe. One link, zero blast radius. Built on Vultr.
